 to)\, Room 108\, 155 College St. Please note: this is not Myhal Centre as 
 originally listed.&#x20\;\n\nTopic: A Data-Driven Approach to Toronto's El
 ectoral Geography\n\nWith colleagues\, Zach Taylor built for research purp
 oses fine-grained maps of historical election results in Toronto and other
  cities. He will discuss how they built the maps\, what they have used the
 m for\, and how spatial data like this could be used in the future.\n\nSpe
 aker: Zack Taylor (he/him) joining via Zoom\n\nZack Taylor is a professor 
 of Political Science and Geography at the University of Western Ontario wh
 ere he specializes in urban politics\, local governance\, and political ge
 ography.\n\nAgenda:\n\n7:00-7:20 Welcome and Introductions\n\n7:20-7:50 Pr
